# AI Car Matchmaker - Cursor Development Guidelines

## Project Architecture
- Framework: Full-Stack Monorepo
- Backend: Python 3.11+ / FastAPI / Uvicorn
- DB: SQLite (Persistent 120+ Car Inventory Dataset)
- AI Agent: Claude Agent SDK / LangChain DeepAgents
- Frontend: React 18 / Vite / Lucide-React
- Protocols:
  - A2UI v0.9.1 (Google Agent-to-UI declarative JSON streaming protocol)
  - MCP Apps (Model Context Protocol embedded UI applications)
- Observability: OpenTelemetry + Langfuse SDK

## Critical Protocol & Schema Rules

1. A2UI Protocol Rules:
   - Always emit flat JSON stream payloads matching A2UI v0.9.1 spec.
   - Message Types: `createSurface`, `updateComponents`, `updateDataModel`.
   - Never output static HTML or raw inline JSX inside agent reasoning streams.
   - Separate UI layout structure from data updates.

2. MCP Apps Rules:
   - Interactive forms (preference interview) and payment gateways (mock checkout) MUST be isolated as MCP Apps.
   - Mock checkout must NOT call external payment networks (e.g., Stripe, BMW APIs) and must run as a safe, sandboxed frame inside chat.

3. Agent State Machine:
   - Maintain explicit state across turns: `INTERVIEW` -> `RESEARCH` -> `RECOMMENDATION` -> `CHECKOUT`.
   - Interview must capture: `intent` (Buy vs Rent), `category`, `max_budget`, `target_date`.
   - Include a "Trade-Off Matrix" in recommendations comparing value vs top rating.

4. Mock Marketplace Dataset:
   - Database must pre-seed 120+ cars across 10 categories (SUV, Sedan, EV, Luxury, Sports, Hybrid, Compact, Truck, Minivan, Convertible) with >=10 brands per category.
